85ml  buttermilk (I just add 1 tea spoon of lemon juice to 80ml milk)
110g butter
225g golden caster sugar
Pinch Salt
2 large eggs
4 ripe bananas  mashed up
1 tsp vanilla extract
1 tsp cinnamon powder 
1 tsp bicarbonate of soda
285g plain flour
80-100g dark chocolate

Fan oven 160-170 (bake for 50-65 mins)
1) Cream butter and sugar together
2) Add in the 2 eggs and mix together
2.5) Add the mashed banana
3) add in the butter milk, vanilla and cinnamon powder
4) Sift in the flour, bicard soda and salt
5) Mix together and add dark chocolate at end
6) add to bread tin and top with crushed walnuts if u are pro like me!
Timing can be a bit off depenbding on ur baking tin, so i just use knifee/skewer to test if wet in middle
but ur a pro
